[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/comments/4132415901","html_url":"https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/13719#issuecomment-4132415901","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/13719","id":4132415901,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAI0trM72T6md","user":{"login":"cdoublev","id":15889080,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1ODg5MDgw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15889080?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdoublev","html_url":"https://github.com/cdoublev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdoublev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdoublev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdoublev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdoublev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdoublev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdoublev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdoublev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdoublev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdoublev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-26T07:47:42Z","updated_at":"2026-03-26T07:47:42Z","body":"To elaborate on my previous comment (after a more in-depth research).\n\n  > > To maintain legibility, the `<system-color>` keywords also respond to light mode or dark mode changes.\n  >\n  > This statement is not backed by any defined requirement.\n\nThis [comment](https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/6773#issuecomment-1098285102) confirms that this requirement needs to be defined (emphasize added):\n\n  > There may be some updates needed around `color-scheme`, as well. (i.e. to **clarify that it affects the computed value of system colors**)\n\nIt was written before the resolution to use the corresponding `<system-color>` value in its colorspace as the computed value, instead of the specified keyword.\n\nHowever, I would expect it to be clarified in [§ 14.5. Resolving other colors (CSS Color)](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-color-4/#resolving-other-colors), which currently only says this:\n\n  > The declared value for each `<system-color>` keyword and `<deprecated-color>` keyword is itself. The computed value is the corresponding color in its color space.\n\nSimilarly, I was not expecting to find the [`<system-color>` mappings](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-color-adjust-1/#forced-color-palettes) in CSS Color Adjustment, fwiw.\n\n---\n\n[These comments](https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/3873#issuecomment-548001301) also suggest that how to compute `<deprecated-color>` is also currently underspecified:\n\n  > Dropping a note here to say: don't forget to say how these values compute, if they compute to other keyword values or to a fixed color or to themselves. (I'm guessing fewer keywords that compute to themselves here is better for implementations.)\n\n  > Given that these are legacy values for legacy compat & we don't want authors using them in new content, we can probably safely define them all as light mode values.\n\nAnd #13459 asked if `<deprecated-color>`s should be (parse time) aliases of `<system-color>`s.\n\n---\n\n  > But light mode or dark mode changes seems restrictive.\n\nI thought other modes than light/dark modes exist tbh. But my point was also that the linked algorithm does not just consider the user preferred color scheme.","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/comments/4132415901/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/comments/4138011658","html_url":"https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/13719#issuecomment-4138011658","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/13719","id":4138011658,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAI0trM72pQwK","user":{"login":"svgeesus","id":2506926,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MDY5MjY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2506926?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/svgeesus","html_url":"https://github.com/svgeesus","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/svgeesus/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/svgeesus/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/svgeesus/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/svgeesus/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/svgeesus/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/svgeesus/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/svgeesus/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/svgeesus/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/svgeesus/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-26T20:29:44Z","updated_at":"2026-03-26T20:29:44Z","body":"[Better?](https://www.w3.org/TR/css-color-4/#css-system-colors)","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/comments/4138011658/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/comments/4140241870","html_url":"https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/13719#issuecomment-4140241870","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/13719","id":4140241870,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAI0trM72xxPO","user":{"login":"cdoublev","id":15889080,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1ODg5MDgw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15889080?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdoublev","html_url":"https://github.com/cdoublev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdoublev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdoublev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdoublev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdoublev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdoublev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdoublev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdoublev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdoublev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdoublev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-27T05:07:53Z","updated_at":"2026-03-27T08:34:02Z","body":"I think so. Thank you.\n\nRegarding `<deprecated-color>`. I do not think its computed value is tested on WPT. ~~If it was defined as a parse time alias of `<system-color>`, as suggested in #13459, this would change the declared/resolved value that can be observed in Chrome and Firefox today:~~ (edit) No, sorry. There was an oversight in my test code. I can observe that the computed value of `<deprecated-color>` is the same value as the corresponding `<system-color>`, so defining `<deprecated-color>` as an alias would only change the declared value :\n\n```js\nconst { style: declared } = target\nconst resolved = getComputedStyle(target)\n\n// ButtonBorder (<deprecated-color>) maps to ActiveBorder (<system-color>)\n\ndeclared.colorScheme = 'light'\ndeclared.color = 'buttonborder'\nresolved.color // \"rgb(0, 0, 0)\"\ndeclared.colorScheme = 'dark'\nresolved.color // \"rgb(255, 255, 255)\"\n\ndeclared.colorScheme = 'light'\ndeclared.color = 'activeborder'\nresolved.color // \"rgb(0, 0, 0)\"\ndeclared.colorScheme = 'dark'\nresolved.color // \"rgb(255, 255, 255)\"\n```\n\n~~This is the behavior suggested in the comment I already quoted in my previous comment:~~\n\n  > ~~Given that these are legacy values for legacy compat & we don't want authors using them in new content, we can probably safely define them all as light mode values~~\n\n~~So do you want to postpone this question until #13459 is answered?~~ Do you want me to open a separate issue? Or do you want to clarify it right away?","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/comments/4140241870/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/comments/4157689875","html_url":"https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/13719#issuecomment-4157689875","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/13719","id":4157689875,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAI0trM730VAT","user":{"login":"svgeesus","id":2506926,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MDY5MjY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2506926?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/svgeesus","html_url":"https://github.com/svgeesus","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/svgeesus/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/svgeesus/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/svgeesus/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/svgeesus/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/svgeesus/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/svgeesus/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/svgeesus/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/svgeesus/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/svgeesus/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-30T19:42:36Z","updated_at":"2026-03-30T19:42:36Z","body":"I agree this needs to be tested on WPT.\n\nI prefer to use an explicit alias, and just discussed this with @Loirooriol but other implementers have yet to chime in.\n\nNot sure this needs a separate issue.","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/comments/4157689875/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/comments/4994913688","html_url":"https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/13719#issuecomment-4994913688","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/13719","id":4994913688,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAI0trM8AAAABKbhVmA","user":{"login":"svgeesus","id":2506926,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MDY5MjY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2506926?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/svgeesus","html_url":"https://github.com/svgeesus","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/svgeesus/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/svgeesus/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/svgeesus/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/svgeesus/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/svgeesus/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/svgeesus/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/svgeesus/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/svgeesus/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/svgeesus/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-16T17:44:58Z","updated_at":"2026-07-16T17:44:58Z","body":"I believe that [this is now clear in the spec](https://www.w3.org/TR/css-color-4/#resolving-other-colors)","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/comments/4994913688/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":